{"type":"message_update","usage":{"input":26796,"output":915,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":0,"totalTokens":27711,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0,"totalFromProvider":false}},"assistantMessageEvent":{"type":"thinking_end","contentIndex":0,"content":"Let's start by understanding the task. This is ticket 31: the `login` paste flow, part 1 — storing keys. I need to do the following:\n\n1. First, use the /tdd skill (the instructions say \"use /tdd to implement the ticket\").\n2. Before writing any code, read the files directly related to the ticket.\n3. Work only on this ticket.\n4. Keep notes in `.redeye/notes.md`.\n5. Commit after each checklist item.\n6. Run the full `npm test` at the end.\n\nFirst, let me load the tdd skill, and then investigate the repository structure.\n\nTicket contents:\n- `npx roast login <provider>` for storing the provider's API key (default is project scope, `--global` is user scope)\n- After opening the provider's key page (skipped with `--no-browser`), paste the key at a no-echo prompt\n- Before storing, verify the key against the provider's `GET /v1/models`\n- Never display the key\n- Targets are OpenAI, Anthropic (paste providers)\n- Shared `loginPath` (scope rules + outside-repo usage error) and `providerNames`\n- Verification uses a swappable `fetch` with `redirect: 'manual'`, and the body is read up to a max of 32 KiB\n- Test fakes are in `test/helpers/provider-server.ts`\n- `test/cli/login.ts`\n\nAcceptance criteria:\n1. `login anthropic` with a pasted key (trimming surrounding whitespace) is saved to the project's `credentials.json` (0600 inside a 0700 directory), and a subsequent review to the built-in endpoint sends it.\n2. `login openai --global` is saved only to the user file, and the verification request includes `Authorization: Bearer <key>`.\n3. The key page URL is passed to `openBrowser` (except in the case of `--no-browser`). A failing opener must not cause login to fail.\n4. Logging in again replaces the saved key.\n5. No portion of any pasted key must appear in stdout, and stdout must not be empty.\n6. `npm run lint`, `npm run typecheck`, `npm run test:ts` pass, and the Go build and Go tests also pass.\n\nFiles to touch:\n- `src/cli/login.ts` (login command, `runLogin`, `loginPath`, `providerNames`, `pasteLogin`, `validateKey`, `keyCheckPath`)\n- `src/cli/terminal.ts` (raw-mode `readSecret`, if not present)\n- `test/helpers/provider-server.ts` (shared fake provider server, also used by the `init` tests)\n- `test/cli/login.ts`\n\nWait a sec — the ticket says `test/helpers/provider-server.ts`, but AGENTS.md says the shared helpers include `test/helpers/spawn.ts` and so on. Let me check what exists. Also, the failed attempt 4 log had an error in `test/cli/login.ts` — a type error where the `provider-server` helper was returning a Promise. That means a previous attempt created `test/helpers/provider-server.ts` that returns a Promise, and login.ts expected a synchronous `ProviderServer`. This time I need to do it correctly.\n\nLet me start by reading the tdd skill and exploring the repository first.\n"}}
